# "At the beginning of your upkeep, if you control three or more artifacts" is an intervening if (CR 603.4): it is checked
# when the upkeep begins and again as the ability resolves. On turn 3 Bot1 has three Moxen, the trigger goes on the
# stack, and Bot2's Disenchant destroys one of them in response, so no life is gained. On turn 5 there are only two and
# the trigger does not even go on the stack. Bot1 ends at 20.

[Bot1 Deck]
Inventors' Fair
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Island x3
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Disenchant
Plains x4
Plains x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Inventors' Fair.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Disenchant.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Life = 20
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 3
[T5 Bot1.Upkeep]
? Stack.Count = 0
[T5 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Mox Jet
